verl -- https://github.com/volcengine/verl
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Carried as the git submodule at `verl/` -- specifically
https://github.com/JamesKrW/verl at `27c51e9`, which the tag `vagen-260812` names so that a
`git clone --recursive` keeps resolving. Its history is three commits
(`git -C verl log --oneline`):

  5083fc5  a squashed snapshot of verl main: a root commit carrying the whole tree, so
           upstream's own history is not reproduced here
  12f79ab  attention_utils.py, qwen2_vl.py, glm4v.py, torch_functional.py -- fall back to
           the Hub flash-attention kernel when flash-attn is not installed
  27c51e9  models/transformers/glm4v.py -- unpack the vision tower output as qwen2_vl
           already does, so GLM-4.1V trains on transformers 5.x

The latter two are the only modifications to verl. Because the base is squashed, a diff
against today's volcengine/verl main mixes them with upstream's own drift.

Portions of verl are adapted into `vagen/training/main.py`,
`vagen/training/agent_loop/`, and `vagen/training/trainer/`, which retain their
Apache-2.0 headers. A copy of the Apache License is in the submodule.

